From d91fe96aea1837db2252f4551377e75e433ffb5f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Craterbrain <58347640+Craterbrain@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 23:08:17 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 68/75] PlaitOS: pocket lock fixes from the GrapheneOS doze
 check

- KeyguardUpdateMonitor: register the pocket callback after mHandler is
  created (the binder callback posts to it; an early state change would have
  crashed SystemUI), make mIsDeviceInPocket volatile (binder thread writes,
  main thread reads) and null-check mPocketManager in isPocketLockVisible()
- SystemServer: restore the stock "final boolean safeMode =
  wm.detectSafeMode()"; the pocket port had turned it into a public field
  with a null check that nothing uses

Checked against GrapheneOS's own changes to the same files (second-factor
fingerprint unlock, face auth prevention, fingerprint mode fix, alternative
touchscreen mode, USB port security, system_server extensions): no overlap
in the changed lines; the fingerprint listen condition only gains
!mIsDeviceInPocket, which is always false while pocket mode is off.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .../android/keyguard/KeyguardUpdateMonitor.java  | 16 +++++++++-------
 .../java/com/android/server/SystemServer.java    |  7 +------
 2 files changed, 10 insertions(+), 13 deletions(-)

